<h1>Components</h1>
<nav role="navigation" aria-label="A to Z navigation">
<ol class="style-a-z" role="list"><% groups = component_letter_groups %><% ComponentHelpers::COMPONENT_LETTERS.each do |letter| %><li><% if groups[letter] %><a class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state" href="#<%= letter.downcase %>"><%= letter %></a><% else %><span class="style-a-z__empty"><%= letter %></span><% end %></li><% end %></ol>
</nav>
<div class="c-search-filter c-component-search" data-component-search hidden>
<label for="component-search">Find a component or element</label>
<p class="c-component-search__hint" id="component-search-hint">Type a component name, a Home Assistant element such as hui-tile-card, or an HTML element such as &lt;details&gt;.</p>
<div class="c-component-search__field">
<input id="component-search" type="text" role="combobox" aria-autocomplete="list" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="component-search-listbox" aria-describedby="component-search-hint" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false">
<ul class="c-component-search__listbox" id="component-search-listbox" role="listbox" aria-label="Matching components and elements" hidden></ul>
</div>
<p class="govuk-visually-hidden" role="status" data-component-search-status></p>
</div>
<script type="application/json" id="component-search-data"><%= component_search_json %></script>
<p>Each component has, or will have, one page that owns it and every element and variant it contains. Pages are being moved to this structure one letter group at a time. Until a page has a section for each element, a search result for one of its elements opens the top of that page. A component without a page yet is marked Specification not yet published. The same list is available to machine readers as <a href="../reference/component-index.json">component-index.json</a>.</p>
<p>An example here does not mean the native Home Assistant interface has been replaced. The <a href="../community/coverage.html">source coverage record</a> maps each component to its source.</p>
<div class="c-component-az" data-component-list>
<% component_letter_groups.each do |letter, parents| %><h2 class="style-a-z__letter" id="<%= letter.downcase %>"><%= letter %></h2>
<ul class="c-component-az__list" role="list">
<% parents.each do |parent| %><li id="<%= parent['list_anchor'] %>" data-component-parent="<%= escape(parent['parent']) %>"><% if parent['available'] %><a class="govuk-link" href="<%= docs_path(parent['route']) %>"><%= escape(parent['parent']) %></a><% else %><span class="c-component-az__name"><%= escape(parent['parent']) %></span><% end %> <span class="c-component-az__meta"><%= escape(component_origin_summary(parent)) %><%= parent['available'] ? '' : ' · Specification not yet published' %></span></li>
<% end %></ul>
<% end %></div>
<p><small>Source note: component guidance is adapted from the <a href="https://design-system.service.gov.uk/">GOV.UK Design System</a> and the <a href="https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system">NHS digital service manual</a>. Specific sources: <a href="https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/hint-text">NHS hint text</a>, <a href="https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/buttons">NHS buttons</a> and <a href="https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/warning-text/">GOV.UK warning text</a>. Navigation, modal and card references draw on the <a href="https://design-patterns.service.justice.gov.uk/">Ministry of Justice design system</a>, and chart and data presentation on the <a href="https://service-manual.ons.gov.uk/design-system">Office for National Statistics design system</a>. The examples use shared GOV.UK primitives or original civica markup. civica is an independent project. It is not endorsed by these organisations, and NHS logos and service identity are not used. The <a href="../community/sources.html">source register</a> and <a href="../community/licensing.html">licensing and attribution</a> give the full list, licence terms and notices.</small></p>
